        "language": "en",
        "bound_author_id": 340,
        "text": "In 1946 Mississippi, respected farmer and war veteran Pete Banning kills a local minister, then refuses to explain why. His silence leaves his family, lawyers and neighbours struggling to understand an apparently senseless act. As the case moves through the courts, the novel turns back to Pete's wartime experiences and the history of his family. The question of motive connects the public trial with events that those around him do not fully understand.",
