        "text": "Ronald M. Baecker examines how digital technologies influence everyday life and the institutions around us. The book considers computing in education, health, media, government and conflict, then weighs questions of privacy, security, inclusion and employment. Artificial intelligence is discussed alongside the choices people make about designing and using technology. The emphasis is on social and ethical consequences, helping readers consider both the benefits of computing and the problems it can create.",
